4,Mixtecan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixtecan_languages,"January 1, 2026 - The Mixtecan languages constitute a branch of the Oto-Manguean language family of Mexico. They include the Trique (or Triqui) languages, spoken by about 24,500 people; Cuicatec, spoken by about 15,000 people; and the large expanse of Mixtec languages, spoken by about 511,000 people.","Mixtec, Tidaá",Otomanguean
